{
  "dom_id": "step-q68123",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "$\\frac{{5}^{4}}{{5}^{6}}=$",
  "worked_solution": "To divide powers of the same base, we simply subtract the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{5}^{4}}{{5}^{6}}={5}^{4-6}={5}^{-2}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate ${5}^{-2},$ we find the reciprocal of the base $(5)$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{5}^{-2}={(\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}=\\frac{1}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{1}{25}\n$$",
